[2025-11-14 02:25:47] Datos recibidos: {"General information":{"UUID":"a6fd667e-2d54-40e6-ae0d-f84350864ad4","Name":"Environmental impact of beef production in Mexico through life cycle assessment","Category":"Agricultura, Silvicultura, Pesca y Caza\/112 Ganader\u00eda","Description":"Intensive and extensive systems of beef production in the Mexican tropics were analyzed. The aim of the study was to estimate and compare the environmental impact of two typical beef production systems in Veracruz, Mexico. A system boundary was established from farm production to prior to transport for consumer consumption, including intermediate stages of product processing, marketing and transportation. The functional unit was 1 kg of boneless and fatless beef. The life cycle inventory was built using information from case studies; farmers, slaughterhouses and retail point managers who provided information from records and expert knowledge were interviewed. The study included cow-calf processes, pre-fattening, fattening, processing and retail. Several impact categories were analyzed using SimaPro software and the ReCiPe Midpoint method for impact characterization. The results showed that for the extensive system, the cow-calf stage is the major contributor in eleven of the twelve impact categories analyzed, while in the intensive system, it is the main contributor to the climate change, terrestrial acidification, freshwater and marine eutrophication. The fattening stage of intensive system, has a predominant impact on human toxicity, water depletion, terrestrial ecotoxicity, fossil depletion, photo-oxidants formation, freshwater ecotoxicity and marine ecotoxicity; the processing stage has relevant contributions to fossil fuel depletion and the formation of photochemical oxidants in intensive systems. Finally, the marketing stage did not have a predominant impact on any category. The results indicated that the extensive system has better environmental performance than the intensive system for nine of the twelve studied categories.","Tags":"Life cycle assessment, Mexican beef, Extensive beef production, Intensive beef production, Beef supply chain, Environmental impact assessment, Beef production in Mexican tropic","Technology | Description":"The analysis was performed using SimaPro 7.3.3 software for processing the inventory, ReCiPe Midpoint (H) method version 1.06. The ReCiPe method was selected because it is an actual and accepted method which uses mid and endpoint impact categories. It uses an environmental mechanism as a base for the impact model; similarly, it allows the quantification of the environmental impacts from specific indicators and was used to evaluate the twelve impact categories. These categories were: Climate change (CC in kg CO2 eq), Human Toxicity (HT in kg, 1.4-DB eq), Terrestrial Acidification (TA in kg, SO2 eq), Freshwater Eutrophication (FEU in kg Peq), Marine Eutrophication (MEU in kgNeq), Terrestrial Ecotoxicity (ET in kg 1,4-DB eq), Agricultural Land Occupation (ALO in m2 x yr), Water depletion (WD in m3), Fossil Depletion.","Code":"MX","Last_change":"14\/11\/2025 02:21"},"location":{"@type":"Location","@id":"3d26b0b1-7065-32cf-a9c0-6c010184c684","name":"Mexico","description":"reference location, sources: ISO 3166-1, ILCD","version":"00.00.000","code":"MX","latitude":23.951,"longitude":-102.535},"processDocumentation":{"LCI method":"Metodolog\u00eda de evaluaci\u00f3n del ciclo de vida seg\u00fan ISO 14040:2006, utilizando software SimaPro 7.3.3 y m\u00e9todo ReCiPe Midpoint (H) versi\u00f3n 1.06 para caracterizaci\u00f3n de impactos","Process type":"Evaluaci\u00f3n de cadena completa desde producci\u00f3n en granja hasta punto de venta minorista, excluyendo transporte al consumidor final","Modeling constants":"Metodolog\u00eda Tier 1 del IPCC (2006) para estimaci\u00f3n de emisiones de metano ent\u00e9rico y de esti\u00e9rcol, \u00f3xido nitroso y amon\u00edaco; asignaci\u00f3n econ\u00f3mica 64.5% para leche y 35.5% para terneros en etapa cr\u00eda; l\u00edmites del sistema excluyen infraestructura y equipamiento","Data source information":"17 estudios de caso mediante entrevistas a productores, representantes de rastros y puntos de venta; datos complementarios de literatura cient\u00edfica y expertos; bases de datos nacionales (INEGI, SAGARPA, SENASICA)","Data completeness":"Cobertura completa de todos los flujos relevantes en las etapas de cr\u00eda, precebo, ceba, procesamiento y comercializaci\u00f3n para sistemas extensivo e intensivo","Data selection":"Incluye animales, pasturas, concentrados, fertilizantes, pesticidas, agua, electricidad, gas, empaques, materiales de distribuci\u00f3n, disposici\u00f3n de residuos org\u00e1nicos y transporte de productos","Data treatment":"Validaci\u00f3n cruzada con datos publicados, reportes y estad\u00edsticas nacionales; consulta con asociaciones ganaderas, investigadores y especialistas","Sampling procedure":"Muestreo por casos representativos: 2 ranches para cr\u00eda, 2 casos por proceso y sistema para precebo, ceba y procesamiento (total 12 casos), 1 tienda de cadena grande para comercializaci\u00f3n intensiva, 2 carnicer\u00edas para comercializaci\u00f3n extensiva","Data collection period":"Un a\u00f1o de operaciones para cada unidad de producci\u00f3n, procesamiento y comercializaci\u00f3n analizada","Use advice":"Aplicable espec\u00edficamente a sistemas de producci\u00f3n bovina en tr\u00f3pico mexicano (Veracruz); resultados no extrapolables directamente a otras regiones sin ajustes por condiciones locales","Completeness":"Inventario completo que cubre todas las etapas relevantes del ciclo de vida con datos primarios y secundarios validados","Sources":"Huerta, A.R., G\u00fcereca, L.P., Rubio Lozano, M.S. (2016). Environmental impact of beef production in Mexico through life cycle assessment. Resources, Conservation and Recycling, 109, 44-53","Project":"Knowledge-based Sustainable vAlue-added food chains: innovative tools for monitoring ethical, environmental and Socio-economical impActs and implementing Eu-Latin America shared strategies (Grant agreement no.: 265927) - S\u00e9ptimo Programa Marco de la UE","Intended application":"Evaluaci\u00f3n comparativa de impactos ambientales entre sistemas extensivo e intensivo de producci\u00f3n bovina; identificaci\u00f3n de puntos cr\u00edticos en la cadena de valor; apoyo a decisiones para producci\u00f3n sustentable","Data set owner":"Universidad Nacional Aut\u00f3noma de M\u00e9xico (UNAM)","Data set generator":"Adriana Rivera Huerta, Leonor Patricia G\u00fcereca, Mar\u00eda de la Salud Rubio Lozano","Data set documentor":"Adriana Rivera Huerta, Leonor Patricia G\u00fcereca, Mar\u00eda de la Salud Rubio Lozano","Publication":"Resources, Conservation and Recycling, Volume 109, 2016, Pages 44-53","Creation date":"2016","Copyright":"\u00a9 2016 Published by Elsevier B.V.","Access and use restrictions":"Disponible a trav\u00e9s de ScienceDirect; sujeto a derechos de autor de Elsevier"},"actors":{"@id":"47a88430-1dd2-4569-9741-8249a6672ae2","name":"IINGEN-UNAM","description":"Instituto de Ingenier\u00eda de la UNAM","category":"Organizaciones de investigaci\u00f3n","version":"01.00.000","lastChange":"2025-11-14T02:22:24.615Z","address":"Circuito Escolar s\/n, Ciudad Universitaria","city":"Coyoac\u00e1n","zipCode":"04510","country":"MX","email":"APadillaR@iingen.unam.mx","telephone":"+52 5556233600","telefax":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.iingen.unam.mx"},"Inputs":[{"is_reference":false,"flow":"guinea grass (Panicum maximum)","category":"A:Agriculture, Forestry, Fishing and Hunting\/11:Crop and animal production\/111:Crop production\/1119:Other crop farming","amount":"","unit":"kg DM\/head\/d","uncertainty":"","provider":"","description":"Forage for grazing in cow-calf, pre-fattening and fattening stages"},{"is_reference":false,"flow":"toledo grass (Brachiaria brizantha)","category":"A:Agriculture, Forestry, Fishing and Hunting\/11:Crop and anim