[2025-11-19 18:19:40] Datos recibidos: {"General information":{"UUID":"6215b98e-7f9f-4f81-a5e0-9f7a67c076b8","Name":"Environmental impact of Oaxaca cheese production and wastewater from artisanal dairies under two scenarios in Aculco, State of Mexico","Category":"Manufactura\/3115 Fabricaci\u00f3n de Productos L\u00e1cteos","Description":"El estudio evalu\u00f3 los impactos ambientales de la producci\u00f3n de queso Oaxaca en cuatro queser\u00edas artesanales del Estado de M\u00e9xico mediante an\u00e1lisis de ciclo de vida en 10 categor\u00edas de impacto: calentamiento global, agotamiento del ozono estratosf\u00e9rico, formaci\u00f3n de part\u00edculas finas, formaci\u00f3n de ozono, ecosistemas terrestres, acidificaci\u00f3n terrestre, eutrofizaci\u00f3n de agua dulce, ecotoxicidad terrestre, toxicidad humana no cancer\u00edgena, escasez de recursos f\u00f3siles y consumo de agua. Se calcul\u00f3 la huella de carbono de 1 kg de queso Oaxaca y se evaluaron dos escenarios de manejo de aguas residuales: tratamiento anaer\u00f3bico en biodigestor o descarga al sistema municipal.","Tags":"LCA, queso artesanal, huella de carbono, aguas residuales, biodigestor, impacto ambiental","Technology | Description":"Se utiliz\u00f3 la metodolog\u00eda de An\u00e1lisis de Ciclo de Vida (LCA) seg\u00fan ISO 14040 con el software SimaPro\u00ae v.8.5.0.0 utilizando la base de datos Ecoinvent v.3. El m\u00e9todo de evaluaci\u00f3n de impacto fue ReCiPe 2016 Midpoint impacts categories. Se realiz\u00f3 an\u00e1lisis de sensibilidad con diferentes escenarios de manejo de aguas residuales y an\u00e1lisis de incertidumbre mediante m\u00e9todo Monte Carlo. Se utiliz\u00f3 medidor de energ\u00eda multifunci\u00f3n WR D-024 para medir consumo el\u00e9ctrico en tiempo real.","Code":"MX","Last_change":"19\/11\/2025 18:15"},"location":{"@type":"Location","@id":"3d26b0b1-7065-32cf-a9c0-6c010184c684","name":"Mexico","description":"reference location, sources: ISO 3166-1, ILCD","version":"00.00.000","code":"MX","latitude":23.951,"longitude":-102.535},"processDocumentation":{"LCI method":"Life cycle assessment (LCA) according to ISO 14040 using SimaPro\u00ae v.8.5.0.0 software with ReCiPe 2016 Midpoint impacts categories method, Herarquista (H) v 1.01","Process type":"Artisanal cheese production system from raw milk reception to product delivery at retail market (cradle-to-gate)","Modeling constants":"Functional unit: 1 kg of Oaxaca cheese; 10% of whey considered as lost and allocated to wastewater; 90% of whey considered as avoided product for pig feeding; Time horizon of 100 years for carbon footprint calculation according to IPCC (2013)","Data source information":"Primary data collected through direct observation and 18 semi-structured interviews with cheese-making personnel and dairy owners over one-year period (June 2018 to June 2019); Secondary data from Ecoinvent v.3 database and Mexican electrical energy database (Santoyo-Castelazo et al., 2011)","Data completeness":"Complete coverage of all relevant flows within system boundaries including raw materials, energy, water, transportation, and waste streams; Milk production stage excluded from system boundaries","Data selection":"Inclusion criteria: All inputs and outputs related to Oaxaca cheese production process; Exclusion criteria: Milk production phase prior to dairy reception","Data treatment":"Monthly production data calculated first, then annual averages estimated for functional unit; Statistical analysis using Shapiro-Wilk test for normality and one-way ANOVA for comparisons; Monte Carlo test for uncertainty analysis","Sampling procedure":"Snowball method for participant identification; Four artisanal dairies selected in Aculco municipality; Triplicate measurements for physicochemical analysis of cheese samples","Data collection period":"One-year period from June 2018 to June 2019","Use advice":"Results specific to artisanal Oaxaca cheese production in central Mexico region; Not applicable to industrial cheese production or other geographical regions; Limitations due to use of generic global databases for some inputs","Completeness":"High completeness for system boundaries defined; Complete inventory of all major inputs and outputs; Milk production phase intentionally excluded to focus on cheese processing impacts","Sources":"Ecoinvent v.3 database; Mexican electrical energy database (Santoyo-Castelazo et al., 2011); IPCC (2013) for carbon footprint calculation; Primary data from field research","Project":"Supported by CONACYT project 'Estudio de productos l\u00e1cteos en el norte del estado de M\u00e9xico a trav\u00e9s de un S-ACV: Estudio de caso de dos tipos de quesos' 4285\/2017\/CI and PAPIIT-IN305620 'Repertorios y estrategias culturales de organizaciones y actores en la sustentabilidad de la cadena agroalimentaria de productos l\u00e1cteos'","Intended application":"Environmental impact assessment of artisanal cheese production; Identification of hotspots for improvement; Comparison of wastewater management scenarios; Carbon footprint calculation for Oaxaca cheese","Data set owner":"Universidad Aut\u00f3noma del Estado de M\u00e9xico and Universidad Nacional Aut\u00f3noma de M\u00e9xico","Data set generator":"Cristina Salas-Vargas, Luis Brunett-P\u00e9rez, Valent\u00edn Efr\u00e9n Espinosa-Ortiz, Carlos Galdino Mart\u00ednez-Garc\u00eda","Data set documentor":"Cristina Salas-Vargas, Luis Brunett-P\u00e9rez, Valent\u00edn Efr\u00e9n Espinosa-Ortiz, Carlos Galdino Mart\u00ednez-Garc\u00eda","Publication":"Journal of Cleaner Production 311 (2021) 127586","Creation date":"2021","Copyright":"\u00a9 2021 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved","Access and use restrictions":"Copyright restrictions apply; Proper citation required"},"actors":{"@id":"47a88430-1dd2-4569-9741-8249a6672ae2","name":"IINGEN-UNAM","description":"Instituto de Ingenier\u00eda de la UNAM","category":"Organizaciones de investigaci\u00f3n","version":"01.00.000","lastChange":"2025-11-19T18:17: